# E §4.3 step 1, L §5.14.1 (tally 2.1.2, issue #38, the user's "A: spec wins, see Jan–May"): a projection's walk
# continues the walk it starts from, so flows of a place over a span that starts before the projection's first day
# counts what that walk booked before it. top tops konto's inflows since y0 up to cap on the 15th of each month: in
# January 900.00 PLN (after pay's 100.00), never again. q projects from 2026-06-01: in it, top on 2026-06-15 reads
# flows(konto, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-06-15) = 1 500.00 PLN (January to May from the main walk, June's pay from the
# projection's), so it books 0; q = 1 400.00 + 7 × 100.00 = 2 100.00 PLN, main's figure. tally 2.1.1's refcore summed
# only the projection's own log (100.00 PLN), booked 900.00 PLN again, and printed q: 3 000.00 PLN.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input cap: money PLN
input wage: money PLN
input dom: int
input y0: date
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount wage

move top[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  reads konto
  leg cash from world to konto amount max(0 PLN, cap - flows(konto, y0 .. day_of(m, dom)))

ask main: bal(konto, 2026-12-31)
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-12-31) from 2026-06-01

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cap = 1 000.00 PLN
  wage = 100.00 PLN
  dom = 15
  y0 = 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
main: 2 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
q: 2 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
